# Feature: a BARE observable inside a local function is GLOBAL.
# Tests:   the two scopes an observable can carry inside one local-function
#          expression, on both propensity paths:
#            RU  unimolecular local-function rule   uflip(x) = kf*Vol*Uphos(x)
#            RB  bimolecular DOR1 rule              ecat(x)  = kc*Vol*Mod(x)
#          `Vol` is written bare, so it is the system-wide count (50).
#          `Uphos(x)` / `Mod(x)` are applied to the function's own tag, so
#          they are evaluated at the tagged molecule.  BNG2 states the split
#          in its generated network, folding the bare observable into the
#          rate expression and resolving only the tagged one per instance:
#            _RU_local1() ((kf*Vol)*1)
#
# Oracle:  deliberately unambiguous, and able to tell the two possible
#          scope errors apart.
#            - Localizing the bare observable (the issue #38 defect) reads
#              `Vol` = 0 at a U or E molecule, so BOTH rules go inert and
#              Uoff / Sub stay flat at their seed values.
#            - Globalizing the tagged observable instead would read
#              Uphos = 400 and Mod = 20 for every instance, running RU at
#              8.0/molecule and RB at 0.4/substrate — both essentially
#              instantaneous.
#          Each arm carries a subpopulation whose TAGGED observable is 0 —
#          U(p~0) and E(e~0) — and those instances must never react, which
#          is what pins the tagged half while the bare half is under test.
#          The enzyme context is a HETERODIMER E(d!1).F(d!1), so `E()`
#          matches each complex exactly once and the per-molecule vs
#          per-complex context-multiplicity question (issue #33) cannot
#          reach the bimolecular arm.
#
# Tier:    network-free.
# Expected (Vol = 50 throughout — nothing touches V):
#            RU  reactive U:  kf*Vol*1 = 4e-4*50 = 0.02 per molecule
#                inert    U:  Uphos(x) = 0        -> never fires
#                Uoff(t) = 200 + 400*exp(-0.02 t);  Uoff(60) = 320.5
#            RB  tagged side: 20 E(e~1) at kc*Vol*1 = 1e-3 each -> 0.02
#                             20 E(e~0) at 0
#                Sub(t) = 600*exp(-0.02 t);         Sub(60)  = 180.7
#          Each substrate is then an exact binomial death process.
# Regression: RM swept every <Reference type="Observable"> of a
#          function-with-arguments into its local set, because BNG2's XML
#          marks the two kinds identically and only the <Expression>
#          distinguishes them.  A bare observable was therefore evaluated
#          at the tagged molecule, read 0, and zeroed the propensity — no
#          warning, mass conserved, trajectory flat.
# invariant: conserved Vol = 50
# invariant: conserved Uphos = 400
# invariant: conserved Mod = 20

begin model
begin parameters
    kf    4.0e-4
    kc    2.0e-5
end parameters

begin molecule types
    V()
    U(m~0~1,p~0~1)
    S(s~0~1)
    E(d,e~0~1)
    F(d)
end molecule types

begin seed species
    V()                  50
    U(m~0,p~1)          400
    U(m~0,p~0)          200
    S(s~0)              600
    E(d!1,e~1).F(d!1)    20
    E(d!1,e~0).F(d!1)    20
end seed species

begin observables
    # Referenced BARE by both local functions -> system-wide count.
    Molecules  Vol    V()
    # Referenced applied to the tag -> evaluated at the tagged molecule.
    Molecules  Uphos  U(p~1)
    Molecules  Mod    E(e~1)
    Molecules  Uoff   U(m~0)
    Molecules  Sub    S(s~0)
end observables

begin functions
    # Vol bare (global, = 50); Uphos(x) / Mod(x) tagged (local, 0 or 1).
    uflip(x) = kf*Vol*Uphos(x)
    ecat(x)  = kc*Vol*Mod(x)
end functions

begin reaction rules
    # Unimolecular: no DOR machinery involved, so this arm shows the defect
    # predates the bimolecular local-function work of issue #34.
    # The tag is repeated on the product so BNG2 maps the molecule through
    # the rule; without it the untouched `p` component reads as a missing
    # component on a newly created molecule.
    RU: U(m~0)%x -> U(m~1)%x                 uflip(x)
    # Bimolecular DOR1: tagged enzyme, untagged substrate.
    RB: S(s~0) + E()%x  ->  S(s~1) + E()%x   ecat(x)
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
simulate({method=>"nf",t_end=>60,n_steps=>60})
end actions
